  {
    "label": "figure_title",
    "text": "Figure 2: Internal stability margin Mint(k; x = 0) for the three entry architectures under the common Gap. The carbon currency (solid) has two stable zeros, the remnant club and the grand coalition, separated by a barrier: it is bistable. The border adjustment (dashed) is also bistable, but its margin at full membership is smaller: the grand coalition holds with less reserve against erosion, which is why the collapse threshold discussed in Section 3.2 is lower for this architecture. The export rebate (dotted) has no stable grand coalition, its margin remaining negative throughout the upper range.",
