  {
    "label": "figure_title",
    "text": "Figure 3: The two-dimensional robustness map. Horizontal axis: ignition cost Hign/γ (log scale). Vertical axis: collapse threshold xcollapse. Each entry architecture is a labelled point; the three regime regions are shaded self-igniting (green), founding-dependent (amber), and permanent- support-dependent (red). Dashed lines at Hign/γ = 1 and xcollapse = 0 mark the boundaries. Filled circles: central calibration µT = Gap(n); filled squares: µT = Gap(n)/2. The border ad- justment's central point sits on the zero line by measurement, not by construction: its collapse threshold is +0.02, the marginal placement discussed in Section 4.2.",
